<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Macedonian dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/867">867</a>–<a href="/years/1056">1056</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Macedonian dynasty ruled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a> from 867 to 1056, beginning with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basil-i">Basil I</a>. Its era saw military recovery, territorial expansion and a cultural and legal revival. The Byzantine economy and state finances were strong in this period, which is regarded as a high point of the empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/macedonian-dynasty.jpg" alt="Macedonian dynasty" width="320" height="397" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: from the Middle Ages, unknown · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Basilios_II.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The recovery under the <b>Macedonian dynasty</b> (867–1056) rested on a smaller but more coherent base: the Anatolian plateau supplied soldiers and grain, the revival of Balkan and Black Sea trade generated customs revenue, and the theme system of military landholding sustained frontier defence.</blockquote><a href="/empire/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>Phokas took part in three revolts for and against the ruling <b>Macedonian dynasty</b>.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/april-13">13 April in history</a></li><li><blockquote>She was the last sovereign of the <b>Macedonian dynasty</b>, which had ruled the Byzantine Empire since 867.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/august-31">31 August in history</a></li><li><blockquote>She was the last sovereign of the <b>Macedonian dynasty</b>, which had ruled the empire for almost 200 years.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/january-11">11 January in history</a></li><li><blockquote>Fearing a loss of influence, Basil had Michael assassinated the next year, becoming sole ruler and founding the <b>Macedonian dynasty</b>.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/may-26">26 May in history</a></li><li><blockquote>He founded the <b>Macedonian dynasty</b>, which ruled for nearly two centuries.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/september-24">24 September in history</a></li></ul></section>
